        <head>couNrY OF CHESTER. DISEASES OF ANIMALS ACT, 1894. SHEEP SCAB.</head>
        <p>couNrY OF CHESTER. DISEASES OF ANIMALS ACT, 1894. SHEEP SCAB.</p>
        <p>Vi °TICE is Hereby Given, that thl Executive COM. mittee of the local Authority of the Couaty of Chester, at a Meetiag held at the Crewe Arms Hotel, Crowe, on Friday, the 29th day of April, 1898. ORDERED—That from and after the 911 day of May, 1898, the Regulations made on the 512 day of August, 1897, as to the Movement of Sheep into the District of</p>
        <p>the said Authority be reviiked. &amp;ND IT WAS FURTHER ORDERED that fr ,m and after the 9:b day ot May, 198, the Movement of Sheep into the Dktrict ot the said L ..cal Authority be ABSOLUTELY PROHIBITED, excepting upon the following conditions, viz. :</p>
        <p>MOVEYIERT OF SHEEP (OCHER THAN FAT SHEEP FOR IMMEDIATE SLAUGHTER) WHEN PUR- CHASED FROM A FARM. I.—Upon a Declaration made by the owner of such Sheep, or his agent, to the effect : (a) That such Sheep have been on the said farm for a period of 28 days immediately before removal. (b) That such Sheep are free from Sheep Scab, and have not be exposed to infection from that disease during the preceding 28 days. 2.—Upon a Certificate of a Veterinary Surgeon ap- pointed es Veterinary Inspector under the Diseases of Anineils Act, 1894, by the Local Authority of the Dis- trict from which the sheep are to be moved or an Inspec- tor under such Act appointed by such Local Authority that such Sheep have been dipped in aVerraicidal Dip within five days before the dace of eateriug the District t f the Lecal Authority of this County, or in the alterna- tive that such Sheep are dipped in a Vermicidal Dip in the presence and to the satisfaction of an Inspector under the before-mentioned Act appointed by the Local Authority of this county within five days after the date of their arrival at the place to which they have been first moved into this county. 3.—That such sheep are dipped in a Vermicidal Dip a ' eecond time at an interval of not less than 14 nor more , than 28 days from the date of their having been first dipped under condition 2. , 4. The second dipping referred to in condition 3to be on the premises to which they have been first moved in this county, unless and except a license for the move- ment of the Sheep from such premises shall have been granted by an Inspector of this Local Authority prior to the second dipping referred to in condition 3, in which ' case the second dipping shall be on the premises to which they have been f erther moved under such license, and within the same interval of time as aforeeaid, pro- ' vided such premises are within the District of the L3cal Authority of this County. 5. Thet 24 hours' notice be given te the Local In- spector of this county of the time when such sheep are to be dipped under the alternative part of condition 2. 6. That proof of compliance with conditions 3 and 4 shall be a declaration by the owner of the sheep, or his agent, sent or delivered within 12 hours after the dip- ping referred to in such conditions, to the police con- stable nearest to the place at which such sheep have been dipped. MOVEMEN i OF SHEEP (OTHEi THAN FAT SHEEP FOR IMMEDIATE SLAUGHTER) WHEN FUR. ufIASED AT A MARKET, FAIR, SALE, OR AUCTION, OR PREMISES 0 THE THAN A FARM. 7. Upen a certificate of a Veeerinary Surgeon ap- pointed as Veterinary luspector under the Diseases of Animals Act, 1894, by the Local Authority of the Dig- trict from which the Sheep are to be moved, that such Sheep are free from Sheep Scab or from any other con- tagious disease, and also upon the preceding conditions numbered 2,3, 4,5, and 6. B.—MOVEMENT OF FAT SHEEP FOR IMMEDIATE SLAUGHTER. (a) Upon a License from an laspecter of the Local Authority of this County. (b) That sun Sheep are isolated and net moved from the place to which they are first taken on arrival in this County, and that they are there slaughtered within 10 days. The Declarations, Veterinary Sargeons' Certificates and Licenses,required by these Regelations must accom- pany the movement of the Sheep to which they relate, and be given up to the Police Constable nearest to the place to wisich such sheep are moved within 24 hours of their arrival thereat. DISTRICT.—The District of the Local Authority of the Count y of Chester does not include the City of Chester, or any of the 13)roughe, either wholly or partly, within</p>
        <p>this County. PENALTIES.—Any offence agalost the ablve Regula- tions is deemed an offence against the Act ot 1894, which renders the offender liable to a penalty of not exceeding TV% ENTY POUNDS.</p>
