        <p>PROMOTION OF POLICR-gERGRANT RARNES.—PoIice-Smr- Reant-Barnf-, who has now been promotel ha. the Chief Constable of Lancaster to the poet of polina Inspector took up his duties at Skelmersdale in the Ormsklrk di- vision on Wednesday morning. Sergeant Barnes who has completed 21 years service has been stationed at Padgate over 14 years during which time he has become well-known and highly respected in the district. Ile has taken great interest in ambulance work in the parish having been instructor of the Church Lads Brigade (Am- bulance Corps) and instructor of the Padtate Ambulance Brigade, the members of which along with the other re- sidents in the village wish him every success in his new office.</p>
        <p>Sununu CONCZEtT —On Friday evening last week a smoking concert for the members of the Institute and their friends was held in the Church House. The con- cert which brought the sesson to a close was well at- tended. Bones were rendered by Messrs. W. Fryer,W. Grounds, J. Price, F. J. Botterfield and J.Harrison. Mr. W. Whittaker also g3VP soveral concertina solos which were much enjoyed. Mr. Frank Blackwell accompanied on the piano. A vote of thanks, on the proposition of Mr. J. P. Critchley, was accorded to all who assisted in the entertainment.</p>
        <p>The news from Freetown,gierra Leone, is very serious. The native rising is of a formidable character, and it is reported that a tswn bag been destroyed and several native missionaries massacred. Volunteers have been enroled for the defence of the colonv,and reinforcAments of black troops and british blue jackets !Five boon or- dered to Sierra Leone.</p>
