        <p>RE JOHN RYLANDS DECEASED. "PURSUANT to the Act of Parliament S.2nd. and _IL 23rd Vic. Cap. 35 intituled "an Act to further amsnd the Law of Property, and to relieve Trustees." NOTICE is HKRABY GIVEN that all CItED‘TORS and other PER- SONS having any CLAIMS or DEMANDS against the estate of4OIIN RYLANDS. late of The Grange. Thelwall, in the County of Chester, and of Bryn Maelgwyn House, Llanrhos 'near Llandudno, in the County of Carnarvon, Esquire, de- ceased (who died on the 24th day of February, 1893, and whole will was proved in the Principal Registry of the Pro- bate Division of her Majesty's High Court of Justice on the 16th day of April, 1898. by Samuel Field, John Paul Rylands, Mark Field, and John James Meekly, four of the Executors therein named) are hereby required to send the particulars, In writing, of their claims or demands to us, the under- signed. FIBLD. SON. and BROMFIELD. on or before the 15th day of June, 1893. after which date the said Executors will proceed to distribute the assets of the said deceased amongst the persons entitled thereto, having regard only to theclaims and demands of whirls they shall then have had notice ; and they will not be liable for the assets of the said deceased or any part thereof, so distributed to any person or persons of whose claims or dens mds they shall not then have had notice. Dated :his 4th day of May, 1898, FIELD, SON, &amp; BROM WIELD. 5. Fenwick-street, Liverpool. Solicitors for the said Executors.</p>
